{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "GuntherToCBMZ",
    "description": "How WRF-Chem adds the Gunther biogenic emissions (GuntherBiogenicEmissions, WRF's `e_bio`) to the CBM-Z species of chem_opt = 170: the GUNTHER1 branch of `add_biogenics` in chem/module_emissions_anthropogenics.F (WRF v4.8.0), which emissions_driver calls for every CBM-Z chem_opt since 2013, when it replaced `cbmz_addemiss_bio`. Every emission goes into the surface layer only, as a mixing-ratio flux over the layer depth (`mixing_layer_tendency`, add_biogenics' `conv_rho = dtstep/(dz8w(kts)*60.)`); the increment over a step is exactly dt times the tendency.\n\nTHE MAPPING IS WRONG FOR CBM-Z, AND IS REPRODUCED HERE AS WRF DOES IT (FORTRAN_BUGS.md B25). add_biogenics reads each species' emission as `e_bio(i,j,p_<species>-1)`: the species' position in the run's `chem` array, minus one. That is the species' own RADM2 emission class only for RADM2 chemistry, whose `chem` order is the RADM2 class order of module_data_radm2; e_bio is always filled in that RADM2 order by biosplit. For chem_opt 170 the CBM-Z order is different, so every species reads some other class: ISO (p = 32) reads class 31, HONO, which biosplit never fills, so the scheme's dominant emission, isoprene, is lost entirely; OLI (23) reads ETH (22), XYL (25) reads OL2 (24) and ETH (19) reads PAN (18), all never filled, so the monoterpenes are lost as well; OLT (22) reads HC8 (21), KET (28) reads TOL (27, empty), ORA2 (14) reads ORA1 (13), CO (20) reads HC3 (19) and OL2 (21) reads HC5 (20) -- the 'RADM only' guard `p_ol2 >= param_first_scalar` is true for CBM-Z, which carries ethene as OL2. Only ALD, HCHO and NO land in their own class, because the first nine species of the two orders coincide (and NO's index, 5, is lno + 1). Two more additions are made because their guards also pass for CBM-Z: KET also gets its own class `lket` (the 'CRIMECH only' block), and the 'CBMZ only' PAR block lumps e_bio(p_ald-1), e_bio(p_ket-1), e_bio(p_olt-1) and e_bio(p_ora2-1) -- i.e. ALD, TOL, HC8 and ORA1 -- at 0.4, 0.9, 1.8 and 1. The component writes each read as `e_bio[p - 1]` with the CBM-Z pointers of CBMZEmissionParameters, so the defect is visible in the equations rather than hidden in a table; the intended reads are each species' own class (`liso`, `loli`, ...).\n\nWhat the tests pin. Steps of the chem170 emissions capture (data/eqwefic/chem170_scm/run_emis.sh) and synthetic replays over every land-use class, asserting every tendency against the real64 replay of add_biogenics compiled unchanged (kernels/emissions_driver), at 1e-9 relative.",
    "authors": [
      "EqWeFiC"
    ],
    "created": "2026-11-12T00:00:00Z",
    "tags": [
      "wrf-chem",
      "emissions",
      "biogenic",
      "gunther",
      "cbmz",
      "chem_opt-170"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "WRF-Chem v4.8.0, chem/module_emissions_anthropogenics.F (subroutine add_biogenics, GUNTHER1 branch), called from chem/emissions_driver.F for the CBM-Z chem_opt values."
      }
    ]
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "radm2": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 41
    }
  },
